@startuml
title CampusFind System - Level 1 Data Flow Diagram (DFD)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #1F4E79
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5

rectangle "Campus User" as User #D9E1F2
rectangle "Campus Administrator" as Admin #FCE4D6

circle "1.0\nRecord Item" as P1 #BDD7EE
circle "2.0\nBrowse & Search\nItems" as P2 #BDD7EE
circle "3.0\nSubmit Ownership\nClaim" as P3 #BDD7EE
circle "4.0\nVerify &\nReview Claims" as P4 #BDD7EE
circle "5.0\nResolve Item &\nCompete Queue" as P5 #BDD7EE

database "D1: Items Store\n(items.csv)" as D1 #E2EFDA
database "D2: Claims Store\n(claims.csv)" as D2 #E2EFDA

' Flows from User
User --> P1 : [DF1] Item details & private clue
User --> P2 : [DF2] Keyword, category, filter query
P2 --> User : [DF3] Public listings (clues hidden)
User --> P3 : [DF4] Target Item ID, claimant proof

' Process to Data Stores
P1 --> D1 : [DF5] Write new item record
D1 --> P2 : [DF6] Read open item records
P3 --> D1 : [DF7] Validate item exists & OPEN
P3 --> D2 : [DF8] Store new pending claim

' Admin & Verification
D2 --> P4 : [DF9] Fetch pending claims
D1 --> P4 : [DF10] Fetch private clue for comparison
P4 --> Admin : [DF11] Present clue vs claimant proof
Admin --> P4 : [DF12] Accept / Reject decision & notes

P4 --> P5 : [DF13] Trigger resolution on acceptance
P5 --> D1 : [DF14] Update Item status to RESOLVED
P5 --> D2 : [DF15] Update accepted claim & auto-reject competing

@enduml
